<title>POLAND: Most Polish minimum T-bill prices ease at auction.</title>
<headline>Most Polish minimum T-bill prices ease at auction.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.202 billion zlotys against a 1.2 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold 996 million zlotys worth of bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price   97.21    95.50    91.18     ---     83.56</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)  (97.26)  (95.52)  (91.18)    ---    (83.57)</p>
<p>   new max price   97.36    95.58    91.24     ---     83.65</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)  (97.30)  (95.58)  (91.27)    ---    (83.65)</p>
<p>   offer	     250.0    200.0    150.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded   122.3    187.8    145.8     ---     746.3</p>
<p>   bids accepted   122.3    156.8    116.7     ---     600.0</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     200.0    100.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
